#
# The Maxwell instruction encodings the shader translator decodes. tools/shaderdec/shaderdec.c turns this file into
# the opcode enum (maxwell_opcodes.h, O_<NAME> in the order of first appearance) and the matcher decode.c uses
# (maxwell_decode.inc), both in the build folder.
#
# One row per encoding: NAME "display name" "pattern" [alias]
#   NAME     the opcode, O_NAME in the translator. "alias" marks a further encoding of an opcode named before.
#            The translator tests ranges of the enum (O_XMAD_R to O_XMAD_I...): keep each family's rows together.
#   pattern  the top 16 bits of the instruction, most significant first: 0 and 1 are fixed, - is either. Spaces are
#            for reading. Two patterns may both match a word only when one fixes every bit the other does and more:
#            the more specific one is then tried first.
# Eden's opcodes the translator has no name for (IDP, IMADSP, VABSDIFF4, JCAL, JMX, LONGJMP, PLONGJMP, RAM, RTT, SAM,
# GETLMEMBASE, SETLMEMBASE) are left out and decode as unknown. Fork additions to the set this file started from
# (DSET, ATOM.CAS, OUT immediate, SUATOM, CCTLT, STP, TLD.B, TLD4.B, TMML.B, TXD.B, VABSDIFF, VSET, VSHL, VSHR)
# match Eden's encodings. Display names go into the translator's "unsupported" messages, which tests match by prefix.

FADD_R       "FADD (reg)"       "0101 1100 0101 1---"
FADD_C       "FADD (cbuf)"      "0100 1100 0101 1---"
FADD_I       "FADD (imm)"       "0011 100- 0101 1---"
